WEBVTT

00:01.500 --> 00:04.837
"It seems today that all you see

00:04.920 --> 00:08.256
"Is violence in movies and sex on TV

00:08.381 --> 00:11.928
"But where are those
good old-fashioned values

00:12.011 --> 00:14.430
"On which we used to rely?

00:15.054 --> 00:18.058
"Lucky there's a family guy

00:18.184 --> 00:23.064
"Lucky there's a man who positively
can do all the things that make us

00:23.190 --> 00:24.941
"Laugh and cry

00:25.066 --> 00:30.154
"He's a family guy

00:34.534 --> 00:37.037
A tragic accident in the Providence area.

00:37.162 --> 00:40.582
A family lost their lives
when they swerved off the road

00:40.707 --> 00:43.709
and into a ravine, exploding on impact.

00:43.834 --> 00:46.212
- Do you find this funny, Tom?
- Oh, no.

00:46.337 --> 00:50.299
I was remembering I accidentally
put my shirt on inside out this morning.

00:50.382 --> 00:55.388
It's fine now, though. So what were
you saying? A fashion show?

00:55.513 --> 00:59.142
Turn the TV off. We gotta find
an anniversary gift for Mom and Dad.

00:59.267 --> 01:02.394
Don't look! We're shopping!
We're shopping!

01:02.478 --> 01:07.191
Kids, you don't need to do anything special
for our anniversary. Just your father.

01:07.274 --> 01:10.403
I hope he doesn't get you a gift
at the last minute again.

01:11.154 --> 01:14.990
My goodness. A human thumb.
Where did you ever find this?

01:15.115 --> 01:19.787
It was on e-bay.
Oh, God! Call an ambulance!

01:19.912 --> 01:22.207
This year, instead of exchanging gifts,

01:22.289 --> 01:25.959
I told him it'd be nice if we could
spend a romantic day together.

01:26.042 --> 01:31.048
Oh, dear. I think we all know what
that means. Boi-oi-oi-oiing. Gross.

01:33.133 --> 01:37.095
Hey, fellas. I got us a tee time tomorrow
at Barrington Country Club.

01:37.221 --> 01:39.807
- Barrington? Wow.
- I'm in.

01:39.933 --> 01:43.060
- Peter, tomorrow's your anniversary.
- Oh, crap!

01:43.144 --> 01:47.106
If Lois finds out I'm ditching her,
she'll hit me with a frying pan.

01:47.231 --> 01:52.736
Which is why I'm gonna drink
this frying pan antidote.

01:52.861 --> 01:55.866
All right, hit me with this. Didn't work.

02:13.798 --> 02:18.096
What the hell?
"Lois, it's an anniversary scavenger hunt. "

02:18.179 --> 02:23.600
"Your first clue is at the Quahog Mini-Mart.
Love, Peter. " Oh, how fun!

02:27.980 --> 02:32.151
Before you tee off, here are your
complimentary monogrammed bag towels,

02:32.277 --> 02:35.488
a sleeve of balls,
and this mobile ball cleaner.

02:40.202 --> 02:44.997
- Clean as a whistle, sir.
- I won't get short by touching your spit?

02:45.081 --> 02:48.127
You'd be the first, champ.

02:48.752 --> 02:53.213
- It's about time.
- Sorry, fellas. I'm not gonna be able to play.

02:53.340 --> 02:58.427
Loretta's mother is in town and we have
to go buy new sheets for the dog bed.

02:58.553 --> 03:01.681
- Cleveland!
- I mean the pull-out sofa bed.

03:01.764 --> 03:06.561
You could be the first black guy to play
this course. People are gonna be impressed.

03:06.687 --> 03:08.770
- Hey, a black guy.
- Ooh, fun.

03:08.854 --> 03:11.775
- Come on.
- Maybe we should play another time.

03:11.900 --> 03:16.780
Screw that. I busted my ass keeping Lois
busy so I could be here. Grip it and rip it.

03:16.906 --> 03:21.282
The fed will be lowering rates, so get
your money out of T-bills and put it all into...

03:21.366 --> 03:23.787
Waffles! Tasty waffles with lots of syrup!

03:23.870 --> 03:26.164
Waffles! Buy waffles!

03:26.289 --> 03:28.667
Waffles! Waffles! Waffles!

03:28.791 --> 03:32.753
Waffle! Waffle! Waffle! Waffle!

03:34.423 --> 03:37.216
OK, kids, keep your eyes peeled for a clue.

03:37.342 --> 03:41.597
What Jughead has done here -
and it's quite ingenious actually -

03:41.722 --> 03:44.223
is paint pupils on his eyelids

03:44.306 --> 03:49.021
so he can sleep through class
without Miss Grundy being any the wiser.

03:49.104 --> 03:51.606
He's sleeping.

03:51.731 --> 03:56.403
- Mom, I found Dad's first clue.
- I can't believe your father organised this.

03:56.528 --> 03:58.905
Usually he can't even handle simple tasks.

03:59.030 --> 04:02.659
Peter, why is there a diaper
in the lamp socket?

04:02.784 --> 04:06.956
Lois, he's done it again!
Wait a minute.

04:07.872 --> 04:09.332
Ha!

04:13.628 --> 04:17.174
- Let's pack it in. There's too much water.
- Let's hit the bar.

04:17.257 --> 04:22.054
Oh, come on. There's worse things
in life than rain. Like... like spiders.

04:22.179 --> 04:24.473
He's behind the door!

04:24.556 --> 04:29.269
Peter, he's bothering
everyone. Say something.

04:29.352 --> 04:32.272
I'll kick his ass.
Someone ought to kick his ass.

04:32.396 --> 04:34.149
Don't go in there!

04:34.274 --> 04:37.068
- Peter!
- All right, all right. Give me a Kleenex.

04:37.193 --> 04:40.113
I knew he was bad. I knew it... Aah!

04:40.197 --> 04:43.116
Out of me way!
They're after me Lucky Charms!

04:43.241 --> 04:47.287
I paid him ten bucks to say it. Classic.

04:47.413 --> 04:53.127
- We'll be in the clubhouse.
- Go on, run away. More golf course for me.

04:55.753 --> 05:00.758
That was close. That looks dangerous.
Somebody's gonna get hurt.

05:05.015 --> 05:07.223
Ah, it'll be fine.

05:14.398 --> 05:16.192
You again?!

05:20.153 --> 05:23.366
- Death, please don't take me now.
- Relax. You're not dying.

05:23.490 --> 05:26.826
- You're having a near-death experience.
- Thank God!

05:26.909 --> 05:31.624
Oh, yeah. Thank God I get to hang out
with a fascinating gent like yourself.

05:31.707 --> 05:36.294
- So, when am I gonna die?
- Two years after your wife divorces you.

05:36.419 --> 05:39.215
What are you talking about?
Lois would never leave me.

05:39.340 --> 05:42.259
She's been crazy about me
since the night we met.

05:45.261 --> 05:49.141
Oh, my God, that's me! Look how thin I was!

05:49.225 --> 05:53.937
My, this is certainly a beautiful night.
I love looking at stars.

05:54.020 --> 05:56.439
- Say no more.
- Peter, wait. I...

05:56.523 --> 06:00.277
Very interesting... but stupid.

06:00.404 --> 06:04.241
Oh, my God! I love Arte Johnson!

06:04.365 --> 06:08.826
- Then why don't you give him a kiss, huh?
- No. Peter, get away from me with that.

06:08.951 --> 06:13.832
- Come on. Give Arte Johnson a kiss.
- Peter, stop it. I mean it!

06:13.958 --> 06:15.417
Oh!

06:24.052 --> 06:26.135
Oh, my God!

06:30.308 --> 06:33.143
Oh, Peter, I hear music.

06:33.227 --> 06:37.607
Yeah, me too.
From now on, this'll be our song.

06:41.152 --> 06:43.237
Ow!

06:43.362 --> 06:48.158
I've never met a guy like you.
You're so full of life.

06:50.952 --> 06:56.374
It's like I can really be myself
with you. I'm so happy.

06:56.501 --> 07:00.547
- Oh, man, she was beautiful.
- This looks awfully familiar.

07:00.672 --> 07:02.965
Wait a second. I remember this.

07:03.048 --> 07:06.593
That's me! Look at all that hair.

07:06.718 --> 07:10.556
I can't believe I thought that looked good.
I must've been high.

07:10.681 --> 07:15.267
- I love you, Lois Pewterschmidt.
- I love you, Peter Griffin.

07:15.351 --> 07:19.648
Look at that. Huh? Huh?
There's no way she's gonna leave me.

07:20.357 --> 07:22.567
Now put me back in my freakin' body.

07:22.652 --> 07:27.656
I can't until you have a revelation.
One of those things that changes your life.

07:27.781 --> 07:29.950
The hell with this. I'm going home.

07:30.075 --> 07:34.456
- You can't get in that way.
- I'm sure as hell not going in the back door.

07:34.539 --> 07:39.127
Oh, crap. I don't have time for this.
Listen, I'm late for an appointment.

07:39.252 --> 07:42.589
If you don't want to follow
procedure, fine. Stay in limbo.

07:42.672 --> 07:46.133
No, no, wait, wait.
I don't want to be in limbo.

07:52.890 --> 07:56.435
OK. It says the next note
will be right under my nose.

07:56.560 --> 07:58.855
They're off!

07:58.938 --> 08:02.483
And quick out in front, Silver Dasher,
followed by My Nose!

08:02.608 --> 08:05.403
Aha! Hold my purse!

08:09.073 --> 08:14.160
- What's Mom doing?
- She's screwing up my six-two quinella.

08:14.285 --> 08:16.665
My Nose out in front,
followed by Sea Biscuit,

08:16.790 --> 08:19.916
followed by Some Crazy Lady
and Middle-Aged Housewife,

08:19.999 --> 08:23.337
followed by Wait a Minute, Who's That
and Silver Dasher.

08:23.462 --> 08:26.883
And now it appears there's
a woman chasing the dogs.

08:29.594 --> 08:33.264
- Let's go, kids!
- Tell the boys in Kansas City the bet's off.

08:33.346 --> 08:38.978
Too late, Stewie. The fix is in
and the noodles are boiling in the pot.

08:39.396 --> 08:41.814
Wait, I got it. I figured out my revelation.

08:41.898 --> 08:44.734
- God loves a working man.
- No!

08:44.818 --> 08:48.363
The Shadow is in reality Lamont Cranston,
wealthy young man.

08:48.488 --> 08:53.159
No! Oh, crap! I'm late. I'm in big, big trouble!

08:53.284 --> 08:57.749
You're shook up about that appointment.
You're Death. What are you afraid of?

08:57.874 --> 09:02.334
Where the hell have you been?
When I said lunch, I said noon, not noonish.

09:02.459 --> 09:06.839
- Sorry, Ma.
- Is sorry gonna reheat the casserole?

09:06.923 --> 09:11.011
- So, who's your friend?
- It's a work thing. Near-death experience.

09:11.094 --> 09:13.304
- Where are you going?
- To take a leak.

09:13.387 --> 09:19.019
Don't forget to zip up your fly. If you don't
zip up your fly, a seagull will get ya!

09:19.144 --> 09:22.897
God, she's a pain in the ass!
I wish Dad was still dead.

09:22.980 --> 09:27.361
Oh, yeah. I'll tell you, Lois's dad
was a pain in the ass when I met him.

09:32.907 --> 09:36.745
- Hi. Can I take my tie off yet?
- Oh, Peter, you look so wonderful.

09:36.870 --> 09:40.292
- You aren't nervous, are you?
- You'll know when I'm nervous.

09:40.417 --> 09:43.125
- Lois?
- Now.

09:43.209 --> 09:47.506
Take the rap for this. I only get one chance
to make a first impression.

09:48.756 --> 09:52.719
Hi, Daddy. That was me. And this is Peter.

09:52.803 --> 09:56.139
Hey, Mr Pewterschmidt.
What are you feeding this gal?

09:56.263 --> 09:58.350
Peter Griffin. Can I take this tie off?

09:58.432 --> 10:01.270
It's a pleasure.
My daughter is taken with you.

10:01.270 --> 10:07.109
And I'm taken with her. I mean, look at her.
Huh? Show us front and back there, Lois.

10:07.192 --> 10:10.320
Don't think I don't know
where that comes from.

10:10.446 --> 10:14.073
That's world-class juice
you got brewing in the old flesh balloon.

10:14.199 --> 10:17.328
- Eh? Eh? Oh, yeah.
- I'm gonna go get my purse.

10:17.411 --> 10:21.998
Based on what you've seen with your wife,
what can we expect in terms of droopage?

10:22.123 --> 10:25.751
Are we talking a slope or full-blown
fried eggs hanging on a nail?

10:25.877 --> 10:28.171
- What do you think of this?
- It's nice.

10:28.255 --> 10:30.341
- It's Etruscan.
- Get out of here.

10:30.465 --> 10:33.260
- No, seriously.
- Oh, that's great.

10:46.315 --> 10:49.442
- Hey, look. A manatee!
- We can use it for soup.

10:54.031 --> 10:58.493
Ensign Glen Quagmire. Welcome aboard.
You picked a great day to get rescued.

10:58.619 --> 11:01.955
We were just about to sing
a song about mopping.

11:02.039 --> 11:05.292
"We're mopping the deck
Which is Navy for "floor"

11:05.376 --> 11:08.503
"And when we're done mopping
We'll mop it some more

11:08.628 --> 11:11.965
- Oh!
- " Swab means mop, deck means floor...

11:12.049 --> 11:14.759
Could you tell me when
you're going back in time?

11:14.884 --> 11:19.974
I was talking to a robe for 20 minutes
before I realised you weren't in it.

11:20.098 --> 11:23.518
Ma, for God's sake,
leave me alone! I'm working!

11:23.642 --> 11:29.149
Don't yell at your mother! If you yell at your
mother, a hen will lay eggs in your tummy.

11:29.274 --> 11:32.693
- Brilliantly choreographed.
- That's your tax dollars at work.

11:32.818 --> 11:34.905
Why not join us and see the world?

11:34.989 --> 11:39.368
Sorry, pal. I've seen the world,
and its name is Lois.

11:39.493 --> 11:43.038
How romantic.
Why can't you find a nice girl?

11:43.121 --> 11:46.459
- Ma, she's gonna dump him.
- At least he got that far.

11:46.584 --> 11:49.586
You know who he took
to the prom? His cousin!

11:49.711 --> 11:51.798
- That's weak.
- Yeah.

11:51.882 --> 11:56.176
All right. All right, that's it!
I'm sick of both of you. Come on, Peter.

11:56.259 --> 11:59.597
Death, put your jacket on
or you'll get frostbite!

11:59.721 --> 12:03.141
- I don't have skin!
- That's cos you didn't eat your beans!

12:04.602 --> 12:07.730
Come on, come on.
Get back in your big, fat body.

12:07.855 --> 12:11.400
Why should I help you save your marriage
when I can't get a girl?

12:11.482 --> 12:13.693
Whoa, wait! What are you saying?

12:13.776 --> 12:18.074
The revelation, jackass! It could have
helped you save your marriage.

12:18.157 --> 12:24.330
But too late. Oh, and by the way, when the
lightning hit you, you soiled yourself. Enjoy.

12:24.413 --> 12:27.750
Wait, wait. I can't lose Lois!
Please, I'll do anything.

12:27.875 --> 12:33.799
- What if... what if I helped you get a girl?
- Really? You think you could do that?

12:33.924 --> 12:38.176
All we gotta do is get you fixed up.
Get your hair cut, give you a good, clean...

12:41.639 --> 12:44.224
...shave, cologne... Chicks'll be all over you.

12:44.349 --> 12:47.561
- Gee! You really think so?
- Absolutely.

12:54.360 --> 12:57.779
You got any SPF-50?
I bleach like a gym sock.

12:57.904 --> 13:02.075
Death, will you relax? The beach
is a perfect place to pick up chicks.

13:02.159 --> 13:06.037
Now, I want you to go over there
and ask those girls if you can play.

13:06.121 --> 13:10.501
- Hey, can I join you?
- I guess. What's your name?

13:12.294 --> 13:14.673
- Josh.
- Do you, like, live around here?

13:14.797 --> 13:17.299
No. I... I live with my mom.

13:18.217 --> 13:23.431
- Let's get out of here
- See ya, Josh. Tell your mom we said hi.

13:23.556 --> 13:25.641
Heads up!

13:27.935 --> 13:30.646
How do we get up there?
Dad put grease on the pole.

13:30.646 --> 13:33.859
Don't worry. We've been
studying fulcrums in school.

13:33.984 --> 13:39.823
You have to counterbalance the weight
at the point where the lever pivots. Like so.

13:39.905 --> 13:42.115
Stewie, you wanna play rocket ship?

13:42.198 --> 13:46.579
- What the deuce?
- Blast off! Go on. Get the note for Mommy.

13:46.704 --> 13:50.249
How dare you use me
for your own personal selfish... Hmm.

13:50.332 --> 13:55.254
Oh. Pull slower. I must remember
to do this game when no one's around.

13:55.336 --> 13:59.092
What was I thinking? You don't know
anything about picking up chicks.

13:59.217 --> 14:01.802
Are you kidding? I learned from the best.

14:04.221 --> 14:06.931
Come on, buddy.
We're dropping anchor in Jamaica!

14:07.014 --> 14:10.769
- Great! We're closer to Rhode Island.
- Rhode Island? Forget that.

14:10.894 --> 14:12.854
I'm taking you out for shore leave.

14:12.981 --> 14:15.149
- Does this look like a "Q" to you?
- No.

14:15.275 --> 14:19.653
- How about now?
- Your crotch just looks like Lois to me.

14:19.737 --> 14:23.825
Let's ask her then. Lois, should Peter
sit around and mope all night?

14:25.367 --> 14:29.122
Or should Peter go out with his buddy
and have some fun?

14:29.247 --> 14:31.416
All right!

14:33.710 --> 14:36.420
That one's a feminist type,
she's into he-men,

14:36.546 --> 14:39.757
and that one's mad for jazz. Watch this.

14:39.882 --> 14:43.928
The plight of women is deplorable.
I can bench-press 800 pounds.

14:44.052 --> 14:46.764
You, me and Coltrane till dawn.

14:46.848 --> 14:49.557
There you go, Peter.
One for you, two for me.

14:49.683 --> 14:51.770
You guys go on without me.

15:00.110 --> 15:03.655
- So why didn't you go with them?
- You don't know what it's like in love.

15:03.739 --> 15:07.075
Oh, yeah? Her name's Amy.
She works at a pet store.

15:07.200 --> 15:11.247
I met her last summer when her dad
hung himself. I was too shy to ask her out.

15:11.372 --> 15:14.165
- What's with that moustache?
- Let me see that.

15:14.291 --> 15:17.921
Sorry. That's Edward James Olmos.
Here, this is her.

15:18.046 --> 15:22.717
- Nice ass.
- Sorry. That's Edward James Olmos's ass.

15:22.842 --> 15:25.845
I guess I don't have a photo.
Trust me, she's cute.

15:25.970 --> 15:27.931
Let's go get her.

15:28.056 --> 15:31.393
- I'll need that picture of Olmos's ass back.
- Oh, yeah.

15:33.353 --> 15:36.272
Mom, hurry! I can't stand the smell!

15:36.397 --> 15:40.861
I found the note!
"Go back to the mini-mart"?

15:40.986 --> 15:44.197
This isn't very creative. Let's go, kids.

15:44.323 --> 15:48.576
Mom, you remember that goldfish
we flushed down the toilet?

15:48.702 --> 15:50.788
He wasn't dead.

15:51.288 --> 15:56.208
- There she is. That's her.
- All right, go on. Just like we practised.

15:56.834 --> 16:02.131
- Hey, you.
- Hi. I was just, uh... uh...

16:02.257 --> 16:06.010
in... in... I was just
in the neighbourhood and...

16:06.094 --> 16:11.433
So I thought that, uh... So... You...

16:11.516 --> 16:15.270
I'll, uh... This is a bad time.

16:15.395 --> 16:18.815
Maybe I'll just come back.

16:18.940 --> 16:23.195
- Who am I kidding? I'll never get her.
- Not with that attitude. Come on!

16:23.320 --> 16:27.157
Robert Reed got Florence Henderson
and he was a burgermeister.

16:27.282 --> 16:29.451
You gotta find a way to make it happen.

16:30.076 --> 16:32.163
So long. I hope you find your girl.

16:32.287 --> 16:36.039
Thanks, Quagmire.
Hope you live next door to me someday.

16:36.123 --> 16:38.334
Hey, does this look like a "Q" to you?

16:38.418 --> 16:40.712
How about now?

16:45.508 --> 16:49.387
So, where is it that you need to go,
my new honky friend?

16:49.470 --> 16:51.557
Rhode Island. That's not too far, is it?

16:51.682 --> 16:57.312
Nothing's too far away from Maxine,
the cheatin' queen. Women.

16:57.395 --> 17:01.065
That's not fair. I'm just speaking out of hurt.

17:04.819 --> 17:08.156
That truck's coming up on us awful fast.

17:09.909 --> 17:12.202
Holy crap! Do you see what I see?

17:12.327 --> 17:16.790
- I'm afraid I do.
- We're being chased by ghosts!

17:17.748 --> 17:20.334
You went through all this to see your girl?

17:20.460 --> 17:24.088
I sure did, and I'm a fat idiot.
What's your excuse, you big chicken?

17:24.213 --> 17:26.926
- Chicken? You take that back!
- Yeah? Make me!

17:27.010 --> 17:30.137
I don't make monkeys, I train 'em.

17:31.930 --> 17:35.892
- Oh! Holy crap! I'm sorry. Did that hurt?
- No. But this will!

17:35.976 --> 17:38.896
Aah! Aah! You bastard!

17:39.855 --> 17:44.860
- What the hell is going on out here?
- Actually, I, uh... I, uh...

17:44.942 --> 17:47.654
Actually, he wanted to ask you something.

17:47.779 --> 17:50.075
Wanna go somewhere and grab a coffee?

17:50.158 --> 17:54.660
- Sure. I get off at two.
- Great! Great! I'll meet you here.

17:55.703 --> 18:01.752
You did it! All right! Hey, who knows?
You might even, you know...

18:04.671 --> 18:07.256
- I'm not following you.
- Intercourse.

18:09.135 --> 18:13.013
- What are you doing here?
- Loretta's mom was hankering for a snack,

18:13.097 --> 18:16.016
so we had to pick her up
some Kibbles 'n Bits.

18:16.142 --> 18:18.519
- Cleveland!
- I mean Cheez-its.

18:18.644 --> 18:21.022
- Did Peter give you a clue for me?
- Peter?

18:21.147 --> 18:23.523
He's at Barrington
with Brian and Quagmire.

18:23.648 --> 18:26.778
He's golfing? On our anniversary?!

18:26.861 --> 18:32.075
Oh, boy. You just put Peter in the
doghouse, which is where your mother...

18:32.200 --> 18:34.285
Don't say it!

18:35.119 --> 18:37.078
Your mother smells.

18:40.623 --> 18:45.337
See, this is why I hate clothes shopping.
I have no ass. I'm minus an ass.

18:45.420 --> 18:48.340
You're trying too hard.
She won't care what you wear.

18:48.465 --> 18:52.219
She's just gonna be glad to see you.
That's how it was with Lois.

18:59.517 --> 19:02.647
Oh, God! Oh, God! Oh, God!

19:07.109 --> 19:09.820
- Hi, Mr Pewterschmidt.
- What are you doing here?

19:09.945 --> 19:14.408
It's a long story - with terrific performances
and a wonderful scene in a carnival.

19:14.534 --> 19:17.037
I'll cut to the ending. I want to marry Lois!

19:17.121 --> 19:20.165
Out of the question! Now, listen, Griffin.

19:20.248 --> 19:23.709
I want you to take this
and stay away from my daughter for ever.

19:23.793 --> 19:27.130
- A million dollars?
- A million dollars.

19:27.255 --> 19:32.343
No deal. Lois may be worth a million to you,
but to me, she's worthless.

19:32.469 --> 19:36.096
- I love her, Mr Pewterschmidt.
- Oh, Peter!

19:38.515 --> 19:42.894
Holy crap! Back then I gave up
a million bucks just to be with Lois.

19:42.978 --> 19:46.941
Now I won't even miss a golf game
to spend our anniversary together.

19:47.066 --> 19:49.986
- No wonder she's gonna dump me.
- Or is she?

19:50.069 --> 19:54.447
Wait a minute. That's my revelation.
I gotta pay more attention to my wife!

19:54.572 --> 19:57.992
Eureka. Now, come on back
to the golf course. I've got a date.

19:58.118 --> 20:03.540
Death, wait, wait, wait. Before we go,
I need you to do me one more favour.

20:05.208 --> 20:09.046
Peter. Peter Frampton.

20:09.172 --> 20:13.550
Oh, no! God, please no!
I'm too young to die!

20:13.635 --> 20:16.345
Sure you're not supposed
to get Keith Richards?

20:16.471 --> 20:22.185
All right. If you want to live, come with me.
And bring your guitar.

20:22.311 --> 20:26.897
And bring that thing you use to make it go
wah... wah-wah-wah-wah-wah.

20:28.440 --> 20:30.526
Hey! Get out of the way!

20:33.155 --> 20:36.490
Damn. How could he lie to me
on our anniversary?

20:58.888 --> 21:03.892
- Oh, Peter. Our song.
- Happy anniversary, Lois.

21:04.018 --> 21:09.941
This is the most romantic gift you've ever
given me. How did you put this together?

21:10.066 --> 21:15.364
I had a little help...
from a very special friend.

21:16.614 --> 21:19.325
- I like animals.
- Uh-huh.

21:19.450 --> 21:22.245
Cos they're like people, little furry people.

21:22.371 --> 21:25.916
Yeah... Hey, you ever go on the Internet?

21:26.000 --> 21:29.043
They got some cool stuff
there on that Internet.

21:29.126 --> 21:33.840
I bought these shoes from a company on
the Internet, cos they don't test on animals.

21:33.923 --> 21:36.842
Wow.

21:36.967 --> 21:41.222
You know, animals never have war.
War is an invention of mankind.

21:41.348 --> 21:44.976
What the hell are you talking about?
Animals fight all the time!

21:45.101 --> 21:50.607
Not with nuclear arms. You can't hug
your children with nuclear arms.

21:52.400 --> 21:53.525
Check, please.

21:53.526 --> 22:54.526
Thank you for watching «Family Guy» on
www.FOX-fan.ru